  <p>
    This is <span data-field="full_name">{{ full_name }}</span>, faculty member of the <span data-field="institution.name">{{ institution.name }}</span> (PURP). I am writing you this letter because I would like to participate in the <span data-field="event_name">{{ event_name }}</span> Workshop, on <span data-field="event_date">{{ event_date }}</span>, in <span data-field="event_location">{{ event_location }}</span>. L.A. PURP is a National Center of Academic Excellence in Information Assurance Education (CAE/IAE) and we are devoted to graduate students proficient in Cybersecurity among other fields.
  </p>
  <p>
    I am part of the <span data-field="institution.name">{{ institution.name }}</span> as Associate Professor, Associate Director of the <span data-field="department">{{ department }}</span> Department. My main interest attending this workshop is to learn about new Cybersecurity trends, how to efficiently teaching these topics to our students. Also, find about funding, educational, and professional opportunities for our Hispanic students in Puerto Rico. Here at the PURP most of our faculty and almost 100% of the students are from Hispanic minorities. However, since Puerto Rico is a US territory we all hold US citizenship. This put our students in a very advantageous potential position of being able to work anywhere in the USA, including classified jobs. But not least, I would like to increase the underrepresented Hispanic group in the Cybersecurity and National Security fields. The reality is that our minority is not fully represented in those areas yet.
  </p>
  <p>Please find attached a short bio sketch, and a paper intended to inspire thought and discussion about the field of Cybersecurity.</p>
